CORE
main.bash
--show-parse-tree
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^dialect bash$
^    assign x = q"tab\\there\\nnewAA\\x01\\\\'"$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Dollar-single-quotes (POSIX.1-2024 XCU 2.2.4): \t, \n, \xHH, octal \ddd,
control characters \cX, \\, and \' are decoded. Uses bash, as released
shfmt versions do not lex $'...' in POSIX mode.
